{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Tehom</b> — like the sense of the verse: he remembers the channels through which water descends from the high mountains." "And the sense of <b>tehom el tehom kore</b> — that the waters of the channels join together below, in the manner of ושעיר אל רעהו יקרא (Leviticus 16:8). And the meaning is that as he passed toward the mountains, the waters would descend like the breakers of the sea and its waves and cover him in the summer days. And the one who expounds this verse regarding the exile — it is not connected to what precedes and follows it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:35.057007107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}